================================================================================
IMPORTANT NOTE ON DEPENDENCIES - READ THIS BEFORE YOU REUSE src/
================================================================================

The pipeline imports PyMuPDF, which is licensed AGPL-3.0 unless you buy a
commercial licence from Artifex.

The MIT licence above is correct for this source, and MIT is compatible with
the AGPL: you may take this code under MIT terms. But if you distribute a
combined work that links PyMuPDF - or if you run one as a network service -
that combined work is subject to the AGPL, and the AGPL requires you to publish
your source. The MIT licence on this file does not release you from that.

Plan for it before you reuse this code in your own project. PyMuPDF is imported
by 14 files across src/, including src/islp/pagemodel.py, src/islp/figures.py,
src/islp/document.py and src/build_epub.py, so it is not a dependency you can
remove in one edit. Every read of the PDF goes through it.

The other dependencies are:

    cairosvg      LGPL-3.0
    pillow        MIT-CMU
    mathjax-full  Apache-2.0
    ruff          MIT          (development only)
